// Gerardus alignment API
// Version: v1alpha1 (may break until MVP 0 closes)
// Package: gerardus.align.v1alpha1
//
// The contract between the Gerardus service and its clients, first the macOS
// VelocityVisualiser in velocity.report. The service prepares reference data
// for a site (USGS 3DEP aerial LiDAR and DataSF building
// footprints), serves it as geometry in a site frame, and registers a sensor's
// settled background scan against it. Design notes and the alternatives
// considered: docs/INTERFACE-VISUALISER.md. Decision: docs/adr/0007.
//
// Frames. Every coordinate in this file is in one of three frames, and every
// field says which.
//
//   sensor  The frame of the scan the client uploads: velocity.report's
//           pipeline frame, in which its BackgroundSnapshot and
//           PointCloudFrame points are expressed. Right-handed, metres,
//           origin at the sensor, +Y along azimuth 0, +Z up when the sensor
//           is level.
//   site    Local Cartesian east-north-up at the site origin. The origin is
//           the centre of the site's S2 level-16 cell at NAVD88 height 0, so
//           z reads as orthometric (NAVD88) height to within millimetres
//           across a site.
//           +Y is true north at the origin. All site geometry is float32:
//           coordinates stay under 1 km, which float32 resolves to 0.1 mm.
//   world   Geodetic latitude and longitude in degrees, ellipsoidal height in
//           metres, on the datum the message names.
//
// Poses map sensor-frame points into the site frame:
//
//   p_site = R(rotation) * p_sensor + translation_m
//
// A client draws reference geometry in its sensor frame by applying the
// inverse of the current pose as a model matrix, so moving the pose never
// re-sends geometry.
//
// Site key. A site is named by the token of its S2 level-16 cell, the same
// key velocity.report uses for lidar_sites. Tokens are lower-case hex text.
//
// Reference preparation and serving exclude OpenStreetMap data. Retired
// layer numbers 2 and 4 are reserved; explicit requests for them fail with
// INVALID_ARGUMENT, including for older clients and cached bundles.
// Player identity and authorisation for map edits remain in gerardus.map.v1alpha1.

